          "start_ms": null,
          "status": "needs-review",
          "text": "Description: A person testifies to successive observations of a bright light in the sky in April 2012. On April 2, the witness made an unaided visual observation followed by a binocular observation. The witness states that for several consecutive days, they observed in the evening a very bright object that gently descended towards the horizon and disappeared around 0:30. This rate of movement undeniably suggests an astronomical body, similar to the setting sun. At that time, Venus, particularly bright (magnitude -5.2), was noted in the evening sky. The object's shapes described by the witness are likely the result of an over-interpretation of visual or optical defects highlighted by the nocturnal observation of a very bright point. The GEIPAN classifies this case as \"A\", an observation of particularly bright Venus during those nights.",
          "translation_text_sha256": "d1bc85b64496512c2683edfffa142a757860b9c3edbf0fa4bf92a6eeac1e3597"
        }
